# Claude Code auto-memory. Conversation-derived notes (user, feedback, project,
# reference) that Claude writes without prompting, and
# ~/.claude/projects/<repo>/memory is symlinked here — so turning auto-memory on
# materializes them inside the worktree. Client-derived detail must never reach
# a commit, and the entry goes in before the feature is enabled so there is no
# window where the notes land unignored.
.claude/memory/
# Agent skills: IGNORE BY DEFAULT, then re-include the ones this repo owns.
#
# This was a hand-maintained list of personal and plugin skills to ignore, one
# name per line. Such a list drifts by construction: every plugin install or
# `skillify pull` drops new directories here, each absent from the list, so they
# pile up in `git status` and can fail `format:check` on files this repo does not
# own and cannot fix. That has happened twice. Inverting the default fixes the
# class rather than the instance — a newly installed skill is invisible until
# someone deliberately re-includes it.
#
# The old list also carried a second reason worth keeping: tracking a
# machine-local skill enrols it in `lint:docs`, whose file set comes from
# `git ls-files`, so a note about this laptop's terminal would become a CI gate
# on a repo it says nothing about.
#
# THE NEGATIONS ARE NOT PROTECTING WHAT IS ALREADY COMMITTED. `.gitignore` never
# untracks anything, so all 31 tracked skills stay tracked with or without them.
# They exist so a file ADDED INSIDE a repo-owned skill — a `references/` doc, a
# second markdown file — still appears in `git status` instead of being silently
# swallowed. That silent swallowing is the one regression this arrangement could
# introduce, and the negations are what prevent it.
#
# Adding a repo skill means adding its negation below. That is the trade: one
# deliberate line when THIS REPO gains a skill, instead of one reactive line
# every time THIS MACHINE does.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/hhvc-*/
!.claude/skills/HHVC_manager_review_current_tool_package/
!.claude/skills/claude-handoff/
!.claude/skills/deploy-paused-feature-coordination/
!.claude/skills/git-guardrails-claude-code/
!.claude/skills/karl-notes-drift-check/
!.claude/skills/loop-me/
!.claude/skills/migrate-to-shoehorn/
!.claude/skills/multi-session-git-coordination/
!.claude/skills/remove-ai-slop/
!.claude/skills/scaffold-exercises/
!.claude/skills/setup-pre-commit/
!.claude/skills/setup-ts-deep-modules/
!.claude/skills/ship/
!.claude/skills/stacked-branch-coordination/
!.claude/skills/unresolved-register/
!.claude/skills/verify/
!.claude/skills/verify-railway-backend/
!.claude/skills/writing-beats/
!.claude/skills/writing-fragments/
!.claude/skills/writing-shape/
agent-evals-regression-gate/agent-evals-regression-gate/SKILL.md

# Scratch capture of a `bun run test` run, redirected to the repo root rather
# than the scratchpad. 197 KB of console output with no reader — the suite
# regenerates it on demand, and a stale copy of a passing run is exactly the
# kind of artifact that gets mistaken for evidence later.
/test_output.txt

# One-off capture output from the build_scripts/audit/ crawlers and a Figma
# token export — ~7,000 lines of machine-written fixtures that nothing in the
# build, the tests or the app reads. `data/page_inventory.*` is already ignored
# above for the same reason; these were simply missed, which is not a harmless
# omission: commit 594cec9 untracked exactly these seven files after a
# `git add -A` swept them in, and with no ignore rule a later `git add -A` put
# every one of them straight back. An ignore entry is what makes that
# correction hold rather than needing to be made again.
/data/audit_fixtures/
/data/figma-tokens.json
/data/figma-components-kit.svg
/data/figma-swatches.svg
